    "How people's words map onto Kung Fu Tea's option set. Edit this file, not the code.",
    "Keys on the left are normalised for comparison: lowercased, punctuation to spaces,",
    "% kept. So 'Half Sweet!' matches the key 'half sweet'.",
    "Values on the right are canonical STORE-LEVEL labels, not per-item literals:",
    "'Large', never 'Large .7'. app/matcher.py walks the second arrow per item.",
    "Anything naming a real menu string is checked by `python3 -m app.mapping`."
